# Override of /usr/lib/pam.d/kde-fingerprint (Plasma lock screen / unlock).
#
# Identical to the vendor file except pam_fprintd carries max-tries and timeout.
# Added 2026-08-22: the same options were applied to sudo, sddm, login and
# polkit-1 and this file was missed -- which is the one that matters most, since
# the lock screen is where most fingerprint verifies happen.
#
# Kept verbatim from the vendor file, deliberately:
#   * pam_faillock preauth comes BEFORE pam_fprintd here, so a locked account
#     cannot be unlocked by fingerprint. The other four stacks have fprintd
#     first, which bypasses faillock. That difference predates this change and
#     is left alone rather than silently altered -- see docs/system/pam.md.
#   * "required" rather than "sufficient": this stack is fingerprint-only and
#     Plasma runs it alongside the password stack, so it must not short-circuit.
auth       required                    pam_shells.so
auth       requisite                   pam_nologin.so
auth       requisite                   pam_faillock.so      preauth
-auth      required                    pam_fprintd.so       max-tries=5 timeout=45
auth       optional                    pam_permit.so
auth       required                    pam_env.so
account    include                     system-local-login
password   required                    pam_deny.so
session    include                     system-local-login
